# Playwright BDD E2E Rules

## ⚠️ CRITICAL: Step Registry

**NEVER use grep, ripgrep, or file search to find step definitions.** This project uses a custom step registry system.

- Search for existing steps: `pnpm registry:search --step "add to cart"`
- Search for page objects: `pnpm registry:search --page "checkout"`
- Search for elements: `pnpm registry:search --element "submit button"`
- Search for features: `pnpm registry:search --feature "wishlist"`
- Regenerate after changes: `pnpm registry:gen`

The registry (`src/.step-registry.json`) is generated by TypeScript AST parsing and indexes all steps (regex patterns, types, params, page object refs), pages (class, elements, methods), and features (tags, scenarios).

**ALWAYS search the registry before writing a new step.** Reuse existing steps whenever possible.

## BDD Pipeline

```
.feature files → bddgen → .features-gen/ (auto-generated) → Playwright test runner
```

- Run tests: `./scripts/run-tests.sh -e <env> -l <locale> -t <tags> -b <browser>`
- Generate test files: `pnpm exec bddgen`
- The `.features-gen/` directory is auto-generated. NEVER edit files in it.

## Run Modes

The test runner supports multiple modes via `RUN_MODE` env var:
- `e2e` (default) — full end-to-end against real environments (Playwright)
- `ui` — UI tests with WireMock-mocked backend (deterministic, fast)
- `functional` — functional/API-level tests
- `dynamoDB` — data layer tests against DynamoDB

Usage: `RUN_MODE=<mode> ./scripts/run-tests.sh -e <env> -l <locale> -t <tags>`

## Test Frameworks

This repo uses **two** browser automation tools:
- **Playwright** (primary) — all new e2e/ui tests use Playwright via `playwright-bdd`
- **WebdriverIO** (legacy) — some older tests still use WebdriverIO with `@wdio/allure-reporter`. Do not write new WebdriverIO tests; prefer Playwright for all new work.

## Layering (respect the boundaries)
- `src/features/` — Gherkin `.feature` files organized by type: `e2e/`, `ui/` (WireMock mocked), `dynamoDB/`.
- `src/steps/` — step definitions. Glue Gherkin to page objects. No raw selectors here.
- `src/pages/` — Page Object Model. Locators + actions. NO assertions inside actions.
- `src/utils/` — shared utilities: `pwHelper`, `assert`, `localeCheck`, `cookieHelper`, `randomData`, `retryHelper`.
- `src/services/` — external service integrations: AWS/DynamoDB, CommerceTools, Gmail, Optimizely.
- `src/fixtures/` — test data (products.json, store_locations.json, stock data).
- `src/mock/` — WireMock mappings and response files.
- Dependencies flow one way: features → steps → pages → utils/services/fixtures.

## Step definitions — regex only
- Steps use regex patterns ONLY: `Given(/^I am on the (.+) page$/, async ({}, page: string) => { ... })`.
- **NEVER use Cucumber expressions** (e.g. `Given('I am on the {word} page', ...)`). They are FORBIDDEN.
- Step patterns are created via `createBdd()` from `playwright-bdd`.
- One assertion-of-intent per `Then` step.

## Page Object pattern
- Every page object extends `BasePage`.
- Define selectors in the `elements` object property (not as class fields or constructor assignments).
- All browser interactions go through the `pwHelper` singleton — NEVER use direct `page.*` calls.
- Export page objects as singletons (one instance per page, registered in `src/pages/index.ts` barrel).

```typescript
// Example pattern
import { BasePage } from './BasePage';
import { pwHelper } from '../utils/pwHelper';

class CheckoutPage extends BasePage {
  elements = {
    submitButton: '[data-testid="checkout-submit"]',
    totalPrice: '[data-testid="total-price"]',
  };

  async submitOrder() {
    // pwHelper takes a Locator — wrap the element string at the call site
    await pwHelper.click(this.locator(this.elements.submitButton));
  }
}
export const checkoutPage = new CheckoutPage();
```

- A flow's first step opens the page: `await checkoutPage.open(page)` hands the `page` to the `pwHelper` singleton; later calls ride it.

## DOM sight (see the `dom-sight` skill)
- Before writing or repairing ANY selector, get evidence from the real DOM: Playwright MCP `browser_snapshot` (when `.cursor/mcp.json` has the `playwright` server), codegen recording, or a one-off locator probe / trace snapshot.
- The MCP browser session has no test auth cookies — for auth-gated screens drive login through MCP, use codegen, or read the failure trace's DOM snapshots.
- NEVER guess at selectors. One selector per element — never fallback chains.

## Cross-step state
- Share state between steps via `global.*` properties (e.g. `global.orderId = '123'`).
- Do NOT use module-level variables or closures for cross-step state.
- Clean up global state in `After` hooks.

## WireMock service mocking
- `src/mock/` contains WireMock mappings and response files.
- UI tests (`src/features/ui/`) use WireMock (Docker) to mock backend services for deterministic testing.
- E2E tests (`src/features/e2e/`) hit real environments (no mocking).

## Selectors
- Prefer `data-testid` attributes for stability.
- Use accessibility-first locators (`getByRole`, `getByLabel`) when test IDs are not available.
- NEVER use brittle CSS chains or XPath. They break on markup churn.
- Define locators once on the page object's `elements`; reference them everywhere else.

## Waiting & assertions
- NEVER use `page.waitForTimeout(...)` or arbitrary sleeps.
- Rely on Playwright auto-waiting assertions: `expect(locator).toBeVisible()`, `.toHaveText()`, `.toBeEnabled()`.
- Wait for state, not time.

## Determinism & parallel safety
- Tests must be independent and runnable in any order.
- Use unique, isolated data per run (timestamped/UUID-suffixed).
- Never depend on execution order or data from another test.

## Tagging
- **Line 1 of every `.feature` is the feature-level domain tag** (`@checkout`, `@account`, `@wishlist`, `@plp`).
- Scenario tags: priority (`@regression` or `@sanity`), locale modifiers where relevant (`@auOnly`), `@wip` for in-progress work.
- **Jira ticket tags are allowed** for traceability (e.g. `@CON-2633`) alongside — not instead of — the selection tags.
- `@skip` excludes from all runs (the runner auto-excludes it). `@quarantine` marks a flaky test parked by `/ko-e2e-heal` escalation — CI excludes it; it is tracked debt, not a fix.
- There is no `@smoke` tag in this family — the fast set is selected via `@sanity`.
- CI selects subsets by tag expression.

## Auth & secrets
- Tests register accounts through the **live UI** (TOTP MFA included) and reuse sessions by **injecting cookies via the cookie helper**. This family does NOT use `storageState` files — there is no `.auth/` directory.
- Secrets are vault-encrypted; the privacy hook blocks reading them. NEVER read `.env` files — use the runtime helpers that consume decrypted config.

## Reporting
- Allure report + Cucumber HTML/JSON reports generated by the test runner script.
- BrowserStack for cross-browser testing (use `-r browserstack` flag).
- GitHub Actions CI with composite actions for parallelization.

## Commit format
- Conventional Commits: `type: short message` — types `feat|fix|docs|style|refactor|perf|test|build|ci|chore|revert` (this family allows `perf`/`style`, unlike other archetypes). Jira ticket in the subject is optional, not enforced.
- Pre-commit `lint-staged` regenerates the step registry on `*.feature`/`*.steps.ts`/`*.page.ts` changes — don't hand-edit `.step-registry.json`.

## Coexistence with existing config
- This repo may already have its own `.cursor/rules/` and `.cursor/skills/`. Kit-installed files use a `ko-` prefix to avoid conflicts.
- Repo-specific rules take precedence over kit defaults.
